### Readiness: OUT_OF_SERVICE while the first model trains, UP once scoring is available
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health/readiness

### Data analysis: size, fraud rate, fraud by category, and fraud compared with legitimate transactions
GET http://localhost:8080/api/data/summary

### Model information and evaluation on the test split (synthetic data)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/model

### Score a suspicious transaction -> expected fraud: true
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/assess
Content-Type: application/json

{"transactionId": "tx-1001", "amount": 2499.99, "customerAvgAmount": 45.0, "hourOfDay": 3,
 "merchantCategory": "ELECTRONICS", "distanceFromHomeKm": 850, "distanceFromLastTransactionKm": 790,
 "minutesSinceLastTransaction": 12, "transactionsLast24h": 11, "failedAttemptsLast24h": 3, "accountAgeDays": 400,
 "cardNotPresent": true, "usedChip": false, "usedPin": false, "foreignTransaction": true, "newDevice": true,
 "newMerchant": true}

### Score an ordinary transaction -> expected fraud: false
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/assess
Content-Type: application/json

{"transactionId": "tx-1002", "amount": 42.10, "customerAvgAmount": 55.0, "hourOfDay": 13,
 "merchantCategory": "GROCERY", "distanceFromHomeKm": 3.2, "distanceFromLastTransactionKm": 2.5,
 "minutesSinceLastTransaction": 720, "transactionsLast24h": 2, "failedAttemptsLast24h": 0, "accountAgeDays": 1500,
 "cardNotPresent": false, "usedChip": true, "usedPin": true, "foreignTransaction": false, "newDevice": false,
 "newMerchant": false}

### Score several transactions at once (up to 1,000)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/assess/batch
Content-Type: application/json

[{"transactionId": "tx-1003", "amount": 18.50, "customerAvgAmount": 25.0, "hourOfDay": 9,
  "merchantCategory": "RESTAURANT", "distanceFromHomeKm": 1.2, "distanceFromLastTransactionKm": 0.8,
  "minutesSinceLastTransaction": 300, "transactionsLast24h": 3, "failedAttemptsLast24h": 0, "accountAgeDays": 900,
  "cardNotPresent": false, "usedChip": true, "usedPin": false, "foreignTransaction": false, "newDevice": false,
  "newMerchant": false},
 {"transactionId": "tx-1004", "amount": 4.99, "customerAvgAmount": 60.0, "hourOfDay": 2,
  "merchantCategory": "DIGITAL_GOODS", "distanceFromHomeKm": 40, "distanceFromLastTransactionKm": 35,
  "minutesSinceLastTransaction": 3, "transactionsLast24h": 14, "failedAttemptsLast24h": 4, "accountAgeDays": 700,
  "cardNotPresent": true, "usedChip": false, "usedPin": false, "foreignTransaction": false, "newDevice": true,
  "newMerchant": true}]

### Invalid request: negative amount and hour 30 -> 400 with each invalid field
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/assess
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": -5, "hourOfDay": 30}

### A generated example transaction to experiment with
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/sample?fraud=true

### Monitoring: report that tx-1001 really was fraud (send it after scoring tx-1001) -> 204
POST http://localhost:8080/api/monitoring/outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{"transactionId": "tx-1001", "fraud": true}

### Monitoring: report that tx-1002 was legitimate -> 204
POST http://localhost:8080/api/monitoring/outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{"transactionId": "tx-1002", "fraud": false}

### Monitoring: an outcome for a transaction the active model never scored -> 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/monitoring/outcomes
Content-Type: application/json

{"transactionId": "unknown-transaction", "fraud": true}

### Monitoring: alert rate, outcomes, precision and recall of the active model, and the last scheduled retraining
GET http://localhost:8080/api/monitoring

### Scoring counter for flagged transactions (returns 404 until one has been scored since the start)
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/fraud.assessments?tag=fraud:true

### Application health, including the model status
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health

### Retrain without permission to replace the model -> 409, because a model already exists
POST http://localhost:8080/api/model/train

### Retrain and replace the model. The old model is not kept; this takes about a minute
POST http://localhost:8080/api/model/train
Content-Type: application/json

{"overwrite": true}
